   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "PERSONAL PLOT\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 8, CC 49 to 64\n   1 Own plot weight\n   2 Own plot meets the main plot\n   3 What they want, against what they need\n   4 Secret\n   5 Closer to or further from the goal\n   6 Questions the audience is holding\n   7 A clock running out\n   8 Who knows first\n   9 What starts it all\n  10 Things get worse\n  11 The reversal\n  12 A choice with a cost\n  13 No going back\n  14 The other side makes a move\n  15 The forgotten plant\n  16 Showing the plan\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 8, CC 65 to 80\n   1 The answer almost given\n   2 The closed box we want opened\n   3 One answer opens a bigger question\n   4 The clue that points the wrong way\n   5 Knowing what they want in this scene\n   6 A rule we learn early\n   7 Asking our question for us\n   8 A hint of what's to come\n   9 Planted early, used later\n  10 The moment that starts it all\n  11 A thing that stands for something bigger\n  12 suite: Hidden agenda\n  13 suite: Chasing the wrong thing\n  14 suite: We know, they don't\n  15 suite: Bomb under the table\n  16 suite: Whodunit hook\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 8, CC 81 to 96\n   1 suite: Two steps forward, one back\n   2 suite: The plan goes wrong\n   3 suite: Crossing the point of no return\n   4 suite: Enemy closing in\n   5 suite: The mystery that keeps you guessing\n   6 suite: We know what they want\n   7 suite: The well-made plot\n   8 suite: Heist caper\n   9 pair: When a secret starts slipping, cringe rises\n  10 pair: When the character is set back, their emotional road drops\n  11 pair: When a scene ends on a cliffhanger, the audience's questions rise\n  12 pair: When the opening grabs with a question, a question opens\n  13 pair: When the clock gets tight, the scenes speed up\n  14 pair: When the audience knows first, every calm moment fills with dread\n  15 pair: When a side story grows heavy enough, it gets pulled into the main plot\n  16 pair: When a side story merges into the main plot, the stakes jump\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 8, CC 97 to 112\n   1 pair: When what they want is the opposite of what they need, they fight the change\n   2 pair: When what they want finally lines up with what they need, they act on what they believe\n   3 pair: When something starts it all, the audience starts asking questions\n   4 pair: When they refuse the call twice, the stakes rise\n   5 pair: When things get worse, tension climbs\n   6 pair: When trouble lands just as it was going well, hope drops\n   7 pair: When the whole plan is told, it falls apart\n   8 pair: When the real plan is hidden, a reversal follows\n   9 pair: When things flip for the worse, the goal slips away\n  10 pair: When a choice costs a lot, the feeling is held in\n  11 pair: When a choice can never be undone, there is no going back\n  12 pair: When there is no going back, the stakes rise\n  13 pair: When the other side moves, dread grows\n  14 pair: When we see the other side's move, we know first\n  15 pair: When the other side is at the door, things get worse\n  16 pair: When a plant is well hidden, the reveal is bigger\nCV-CC 5: MIDI channel 9, CC 1 to 16\n   1 pair: When the answer almost comes, the question gets sharper\n   2 pair: When we want the box opened more, the question grows\n   3 pair: When each answer opens a much bigger question, the stakes climb\n   4 pair: When the false clue points harder, we are misled\n   5 pair: When the false trail is cleared only at the end, the story flips\n   6 pair: When we know what they want, we feel with them\n   7 pair: When time is what stands in the way, a clock starts running\n   8 pair: When the rule is set more firmly, dread builds\n   9 pair: When the rule is broken by accident, things get worse\n  10 pair: When the question asked out loud is never answered, it stays open\n  11 pair: When the hints grow clearer, the planted thing matters more\n  12 pair: When the start hits harder, our questions pile up\n  13 pair: When the symbol is broken, the theme is said again\n  14 pair: When the clock is down to seconds, the cuts speed up\n  15 pair: When the talk loosens up, a secret slips out\n  16 pair: When the plan is laid out in full, something is bound to go wrong\nCV-CC 6: MIDI channel 9, CC 17 to 32\n   1 pair: When it all seems to fall apart, the hidden part of the plan pays off\n   2 pair: When the plan is laid out step by step, it starts to fall apart\n   3 pair: When the lie is about to fall, someone gets hurt\n   4 pair: When the jokes never stop, the story barely matters\n   5 pair: When the night has a deadline, every detour costs more\n   6 pairs: Secrets and lies\n   7 pairs: Questions pull the audience forward\n   8 pairs: Knowing too much\n   9 pairs: The side story takes over\n  10 pairs: Plan to pieces\n  11 pairs: The line crossed\n  12 pairs: Enemy at the door\n  13 pairs: Questions that keep us watching\n  14 pairs: Rules and false trails\n  15 pairs: Seeds and harvest\n  16 pairs: Heist caper: the moves"
   },
